WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.047
Critical thinking is not only an individual skill.

2
00:00:03.047 --> 00:00:05.244
It is also a communication practice.

3
00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:13.676
Reasoning improves when people can explain what they believe, why they believe it, what evidence supports it, and what uncertainty remains.

4
00:00:13.676 --> 00:00:16.653
Clear communication makes thinking reviewable.

5
00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:19.629
Vague confidence makes it hard for others to help.

6
00:00:19.629 --> 00:00:22.534
Good disagreement separates people from ideas.

7
00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:26.715
Challenging a claim is not the same as attacking the person who made it.

8
00:00:26.715 --> 00:00:34.014
In a healthy review, people ask clarifying questions, test assumptions, and examine evidence while preserving respect.

9
00:00:34.014 --> 00:00:41.809
This matters because many errors survive not because no one noticed them, but because no one felt able to raise the concern clearly.

10
00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:49.037
Steelmanning is the practice of representing an opposing view in its strongest reasonable form before responding to it.

11
00:00:49.037 --> 00:00:52.580
This prevents weak rebuttals and performative certainty.

12
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:59.524
If you can explain the strongest version of another view, you are more likely to understand the actual disagreement.

13
00:00:59.524 --> 00:01:04.627
Sometimes the exercise reveals that the opposing view has a point worth integrating.

14
00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:09.941
Peer review and decision review work best when assumptions and evidence are documented.

15
00:01:09.941 --> 00:01:13.768
A reviewer should not have to guess why a conclusion was reached.

16
00:01:13.768 --> 00:01:20.145
Decision records, brief evidence summaries, and explicit uncertainty help others assess the reasoning.

17
00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:24.681
They also make it easier to revisit a decision later when conditions change.

18
00:01:24.681 --> 00:01:29.074
Changing your mind when the evidence changes is a strength, not a failure.

19
00:01:29.074 --> 00:01:34.247
Performative certainty can feel impressive in the moment, but it makes teams brittle.

20
00:01:34.247 --> 00:01:43.601
Strong critical thinkers communicate confidence proportionally, invite useful challenge, and update their conclusions when the evidence justifies it.
